      "title": "Career Center",
      "description": "Career Center | Recruitment Facebook LinkedIn Email X Copy URL If you are unable to complete this application due to a disability, contact this employer to ask for an accommodation or an alternative application process. College Campus Safety Officer Part time ADMINISTRATIVE PT Galesburg, IL, US 21 days ago Requisition ID: 787769 Apply Salary Range: $18.00 To $18.00 Hourly Thinking about a new role in the community? Knox College is looking to hire a part-time, 3rd-shift, Campus Safety Officer. We are looking for someone ready to make an impact & join a great team to work with! Knox invites applications for the part-time, 12-month position of Campus Safety Officer. This Campus Safety Officer will work on an as-needed basis up to 24 hours per week, which may include any shift, including nights, weekends and/or holidays. This position reports to the Director of Campus Safety. Essential Duties: Patrol campus in a vehicle and on foot for the protection of students, employees, visitors and their property Respond to emergency situations and routine requests for service Write incident reports Enforce Knox College rules and regulations Secure and provide authorized access to campus buildings Coordinate with emergency services when required Report any safety/security situations Education and Experience: Required Qualifications: Preferred- two or more years experience in security or law enforcement Valid driver’s license Ability to patrol on foot in all types of weather Strong, professional written and verbal communication skills Ability to make sound decisions, sometimes with limited information, in fluid situations In keeping with its commitment to equal rights since it was founded in 1837, Knox College particularly welcomes applications from members of underrepresented groups. Knox College does not discriminate on the basis of sex, pregnancy, gender identity or expression, race, color, creed, national or ethnic origin, religion or religious affiliation, sexual orientation or preference, age, marital or family status, disability, veteran status, or other status protected by applicable federal, state, or local law in admission, financial aid, employment, athletics, or any other aspect of its educational programs or activities. In addition, Knox College is prohibited by Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972 and its accompanying regulations from discriminating on the basis of sex. The College official responsible for coordinating compliance with this Notice of Non-Discrimination is the Director of Civil Rights & Title IX Compliance. Any inquiries regarding policies that prohibit discrimination and harassment, including Title IX sexual harassment, as well as the policy prohibiting hazing, should be directed to the Director of Civil Rights and Title IX Compliance identified below. Staff in the Office of Civil Rights & Title IX Compliance are  available to meet with or talk to students, staff, and faculty regarding issues relating to this Notice of Non-Discrimination and the College’s policies and procedures. Director of Civil Rights & Title IX Compliance Old Jail 12 | Campus Box K-209 337 South Cherry Street Galesburg, IL 61401 Phone: 309-341-7751 Email: cultureofrespect@knox.edu Inquiries about the application of Title IX to Knox may be referred to the Director of Civil Rights & Title IX Compliance, the United States Department of Education’s Assistant Secretary for Civil Rights, or both. Individuals may also contact the U.S. Department of Education's Office of Civil Rights for additional information. Office for Civil Rights U.S. Department of Education-Chicago Office 500 W Madison St., Suite 1475 Chicago, IL 60661-4544 Phone: 312-730-1560 Email: ocr@ed.gov Inquiries regarding the College’s policies regarding the Americans with Disabilities Act of 1990 (“ADA”), or Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973 (“Section 504”) should be directed to the ADA/504 Coordinator identified below: Knox College ADA/504 Coo