    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=ced18917-a7d8-4729-8bf3-9b2aa345c933&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9206792891422_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Career Center",
      "description": "Career Center | Recruitment Facebook LinkedIn Email X Copy URL If you are unable to complete this application due to a disability, contact this employer to ask for an accommodation or an alternative application process. Archives & Special Collections Librarian ADMINISTRATIVE/BENEFITED FULL TIME Galesburg, IL, US 28 days ago Requisition ID: 787863 Apply Salary Range: $50,000.00 To $60,000.00 Annually Archives and Special Collections Librarian Knox College invites applications for the position of Archives and Special Collections Librarian (ASCL). The ASCL will join a library staff focused on student success and will have the opportunity to collaborate with faculty to develop active and immersive learning experiences for students. The ASCL will also play an important role in developing exhibits and programs that engage the campus community with the library and Knox’s history, including celebrating the upcoming centennial of historic Seymour Library in 2028. The ASCL provides leadership for the Archives and Special Collections and administers its major operations including instruction, research services, exhibits and outreach, description and processing, and collection development. The position offers considerable autonomy and opportunities to build partnerships across the college. The successful candidate will work with the library director to set priorities among these responsibilities while maintaining a welcoming, accessible, and inclusive environment for all researchers. The ASCL also participates actively in the life of the library and the position may include opportunities to serve as a liaison to the history department, take the lead on digitization projects, and assist with the development of Knox’s institutional repository. The position reports to the Director of the Library. Professional development is encouraged and funding is available for conferences and workshops. Key Responsibilities: Directs planning of archives and special collections operations to provide access to the campus community, alumni, and outside researchers. Provides academic leadership for the archives, including developing archives instruction classes, teaching and collaborating with Knox faculty, and working closely with students in engaging with Knox’s history. Designs and creates engaging exhibits on the college’s history and other topics from Knox’s collection. Supports the collection, organization, description, and access of institutional records that document the history and activities of Knox College. Partners with Advancement and Alumni Engagement staff to connect alumni with Knox and Knox history. Collaborates with the Collection Strategies Librarian to ensure collections are discoverable. Supervises the Archives Assistant (currently a 20 hours a week position) and five undergraduate student workers including assigning work and providing training and feedback. Actively participates with library events such as orientation activities and contributes to library planning and assessment. Oversees access to the College Art Collection and collaborates with the Art Department to provide student educational opportunities. Perform other duties as assigned by the Director of the Library. Minimum Education Required: Master’s degree from an ALA-Accredited program in library and information science, or a Master’s in history, public history, or related fields. Minimum Experience Required: 2-3 years of experience in an archives/special collections or academic library or equivalent combination of education and experience. The 2-3 years experience could be from internships or positions held while in graduate school or before. Recent graduates with solid internship and work experience should apply. Required Qualifications: Knowledge of professional archives standards and their application in an academic setting. Engage with diverse perspectives, communicate clearly, and build productive partnerships across campus. Knowledge of, or interest in learning about, the history, mission, and distinctive educational value of liberal arts colleges. Ability to work in a fast paced environment on a variety of projects. Commitment to Knox’s mission of building a diverse and inclusive community and to collecting materials that reflect Knox’s diversity. Preferred qualifications Supervisory experience (student worker supervisory experience acceptable). Experience facilitating research consultations and responding to reference questions. Higher education instructional experience; instructional experience in other environments will be considered. Experience working respectfully and effectively with diverse populations. Summary Pay Range: Compensation and benefits offered may vary depending on multiple individualized factors, job level, market location, job-related knowledge, skills, individual performance, and experience. Please note that pay is only one component of total compensation. Benefits: Health Insurance Dental Vision FSA/ HSA/ FSA Dependent Care Employer-Paid Basic Life & LTD Voluntary Life Retirement Plan Paid Time Off Employee Assistance Program Parental Leave In keeping with its commitment to equal rights since it was founded in 1837, Knox College particularly welcomes applications from members of underrepresented groups. Knox College does not discriminate on the basis of sex, pregnancy, gender identity or expression, race, color, creed, national or ethnic origin, religion or religious affiliation, sexual orientation or preference, age, marital or family status, disability, veteran status, or other status protected by applicable federal, state, or local law in admission, financial aid, employment, athletics, or any other aspect of its educational programs or activities. In addition, Knox College is prohibited by Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972 and its accompanying regulations from discriminating on the basis of sex. The College official responsible for coordinating compliance with this Notice of Non-Discrimination is the Director of Civil Rights & Title IX Compliance. Any inquiries regarding policies that prohibit discrimination and harassment, including Title IX sexual harassment, as well as the policy prohibiting hazing, should be directed to the Director of Civil Rights and Title IX Compliance identified below. Staff in the Office of Civil Rights & Title IX Compliance are available to meet with or talk to students, staff, and faculty regarding issues relating to this Notice of Non-Discrimination and the College’s policies and procedures. Director of Civil Rights & Title IX Compliance Old Jail 12 | Campus Box K-209 337 South Cherry Street Galesburg, IL 61401 Phone: 309-341-7751 Email: cultureofrespect@knox.edu Inquiries about the application of Title IX to Knox may be referred to the Director of Civil Rights & Title IX Compliance, the United States Department of Education’s Assistant Secretary for Civil Rights, or both. Individuals may also contact the U.S. Department of Education's Office of Civil Rights for additional information. Office for Civil Rights U.S. Department of Education-Chicago Office 500 W Madison St., Suite 1475 Chicago, IL 60661-4544 Phone: 312-730-1560 Email: ocr@ed.gov Inquiries regarding the College’s policies regarding the Americans with Disabilities Act of 1990 (“ADA”), or Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973 (“Section 504”) should be directed to the ADA/504 Coordinator identified below: Knox College ADA/504 Coordinator Jennie Hemingway, PhD Old Jail 12 | Campus Box K-209 337 South Cherry Street Galesburg, IL 61401 Phone: 309-341-7751 Email: jhemingway@knox.edu Employees requesting accommodations may contact: Human Resources 52 W South St., Alumni Hall, Suite 100 | Campus Box K-200 Galesburg, IL 61401 Phone: 309-341-7162 or 309-341-7543 Email: hr@knox.edu Students requesting accommodations may contact: Director of Disability Support Services Patricia Harden Umbeck Science and Math Center E111 | Campus Box K183 340 South West Street Phone: 309-341-7478 Email: pharden@knox.edu Artificial Intelligence (AI) tools may be used in certain aspects of the candidate review process for this position; however, all employment decisions will be made by a human. Back Apply Copyright © 2026, ADP, Inc. All rights reserved. Powered by Privacy | Legal | Requirements | Artificial Intelligence To manage your preferences, click here Powered by Please switch to a supported browser listed here ,\n      or some features may not work correctly. Our site uses cookies and similar technologies to remember your visit, collect statistics of visits and tailor our site to your interests. They also enable to offer tailored advertising and to link to social networks. For more information or to set your cookie preferences, you may at any time use our tool « Cookie Preferences » at the bottom of our site. Cookie Privacy Statement Set your preferences Deny Agree and proceed Opt-Out Request Honored Set your cookie preferences ADP values your privacy. We provide you with this intuitive tool to help you understand what information may be collected by cookies, by whom, what cookies are used for and to give you control over how the information is being collected and used. For more information on our data policies, please visit our Privacy Statement.\n\nPlease choose whether this site may use Functional, Analytics and/or Advertising cookies, as described below. Select All Required Always Active These cookies are required to enable core site functionality. Functional Functional These cookies are used to enable enhanced functionality and personalization features. Analytics Analytics These cookies allow us to analyze site usage so we can measure and improve performance. Advertising Advertising These cookies are used by advertising companies to serve ads that are relevant to your interests. Back Button Cookie List Search Icon Filter Icon Clear checkbox label label Apply Cancel Consent Leg.Interest checkbox label label checkbox label label checkbox label label Unselect All Save Changes"
